.TH RESGUARDD 8 "November 2026" "resguard" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
resguardd \- resource monitoring and incident recording daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B resguardd
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B resguardd \-check\-config
.RB [ \-config
.IR file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B resguardd
periodically samples the system's CPU, memory, swap, load and pressure (PSI) and
the usage of every service, desktop application and container (cgroups v2). It
records resource peaks, OOM kills and service failures reported by systemd as
incidents, together with the system state at that moment.
.PP
systemd normally starts it
.RB ( resguard.service );
there is no need to run it by hand. Query it with
.BR resguardctl (1).
If a copy is already running, a second one refuses to start.
.PP
The daemon's logs and the output of
.B \-check\-config
are always in English; the text it sends to
.BR resguardctl (1)
follows each user's language.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-config " file"
Configuration file (default
.IR /etc/resguard/config.yaml ;
if it does not exist, the defaults are used).
.TP
.B \-check\-config
Validate the configuration, print the resulting one and exit. Returns 1 if it is invalid.
.TP
.BI \-socket " path"
Unix socket for the CLI (default
.IR /run/resguard/resguard.sock ).
.TP
.BI \-group " group"
Group owning the socket; its members can use the CLI without being root.
.TP
.BI \-events\-file " file"
JSON Lines file incidents are appended to.
.TP
.BR \-systemd " system|user|off"
systemd instance whose service failures are watched.
.PP
The options
.BR \-interval ", " \-history ", " \-slices ", " \-cpu\-threshold ", " \-mem\-threshold ,
.BR \-psi\-cpu\-threshold ", " \-psi\-mem\-threshold ", " \-psi\-io\-threshold " and " \-sustain
are equivalent to keys of the configuration file and take precedence over it;
they are meant for development.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The YAML file accepts
.BR interval ", " history ,
.B thresholds
.RB ( cpu ", " memory ", " psi_cpu ", " psi_memory ", " psi_io ", " sustain )
and
.B services
.RB ( slices ", " ignore ).
The installed file documents every key. After editing it:
.PP
.RS
.B sudo resguardd \-check\-config
.br
.B sudo systemctl reload resguard
.RE
.PP
Reloading (SIGHUP) keeps the history and the ongoing peaks. If the file is
invalid, the previous configuration is kept and the error is logged. For
security, the file is rejected if other users can modify it.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reload the configuration.
.TP
.BR SIGTERM ", " SIGINT
Exit cleanly.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/resguard/config.yaml
Configuration.
.TP
.I /var/lib/resguard/events.jsonl
Incident log, one per line in JSON (readable only by root).
.TP
.I /run/resguard/resguard.sock
CLI socket.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR resguardctl (1),
.BR systemd.resource\-control (5),
.BR journalctl (1)
